<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sergius IV of Naples</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1036</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sergius IV was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> from about 1002 to around 1036. Driven from his city in 1027 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandulf-iv-of-capua">Pandulf IV of Capua</a>, he recovered it in 1029 with the help of Norman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, and in 1030 granted their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rainulf-drengot">Rainulf Drengot</a> the town of Aversa, the first Norman lordship in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He later retired to a monastery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sergius-iv-of-naples.jpg" alt="Sergius IV of Naples" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. MapMaster assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italy_1000_AD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
